// Storage security rules for per-user attachment folders.
// Paste into the Console under your project's Storage > Security Rules,
// validate, then publish. No matching rule means every request is denied.
//
// Quirks found on the 26.1 build these demos ran against:
//   - The recursive wildcard {file=**} is rejected as "Invalid CEL rule".
//     A single-segment {fileName} matches the attachments/<uid>/<file> layout.
//   - There is no dependable size field for `create`. resource.size and
//     request.resource.data.size publish but DENY every create; and even
//     request.resource.size (which works for a plain uploadBytes) is NOT
//     populated for a *resumable* upload (uploadBytesResumable), so a size
//     gate there silently denies every real upload with ORA-20012.
//     So the rule enforces ownership only; cap the size client-side instead
//     (the app checks file.size before starting the upload).

match /attachments/{userId}/{fileName} {
  // Only the owner of the folder can list, download, upload and delete.
  allow get, list: if request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == userId;
  allow create:    if request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == userId;
  allow delete:    if request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == userId;
}
